        </pattern>
        <rect width="100%" height="100%" fill="url(#dot-pattern-nordictrackcommercial1750treadmill)"></rect>
      </svg>
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 relative z-10 text-center">
        <div class="flex justify-center mb-6">
          <TrustBadge />
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-center gap-3 mb-6 flex-wrap">
          <span class="bg-[#FF5A1F] text-white px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest">
            Model Review
          </span>
          <span class="bg-green-500 text-white px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest">
            Updated October 2026
          </span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-4xl lg:text-6xl font-black text-white leading-tight mb-8">
          NordicTrack Commercial 1750 <span class="text-[#5AA9FF]">Treadmill Review</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
          The Commercial 1750 is the NordicTrack most buyers end up considering, and the machine sold under that name today is not the one most older reviews describe. This review sets out the figures NordicTrack confirms for the current model, what they mean in use, and when the 1250, the 2450 or a T Series machine is the better buy.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-4">
          <a href="#current-specs" class="bg-[#FF5A1F] hover:bg-[#E64F16] text-white px-8 py-4 rounded-xl font-black no-underline transition-colors uppercase tracking-widest text-sm">
            The Current Specs
          </a>
          <a href="#who-should-buy" class="bg-white/10 hover:bg-white/20 text-white px-8 py-4 rounded-xl font-black no-underline transition-colors uppercase tracking-widest text-sm border border-white/20">
            Who Should Buy It
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>


    <!-- Author & Meta -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pt-12">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4 py-8 border-b border-gray-100">
        <img src="/authors/shaheer-ali-khan.png" alt="Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD" width="48" height="48" class="w-12 h-12 rounded-full" />
        <div>
          <p class="font-bold text-gray-900 leading-tight"><a href="/editorial-standards/#who" rel="author" class="text-gray-900 no-underline hover:underline">Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD</a></p>
          <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm leading-tight">Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist · ACSM-EP, CSCS</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hidden sm:block w-px h-8 bg-gray-200"></div>
        <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm">
          Last Updated: <strong class="text-gray-700">October 14, 2026</strong>
        </p>
        <div class="ml-auto">
          <SocialProof users="1.9k" />
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="not-prose my-10 bg-blue-50 border border-blue-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 m-0 leading-relaxed">
          <strong class="text-gray-900">What we checked, and what we have not done.</strong> On
          14 October 2026 we read NordicTrack's US product page for the Commercial 1750 (SKU
          NTL17125), including its specification tables, warranty text and footnotes, and
          cross-checked it against P.C. Richard &amp; Son's listing and Costco's listing for the same
          model number. NordicTrack and P.C. Richard agree on the 4.25 CHP motor rating, the
          22 x 60 in. belt, the 400 lb maximum user weight, the 0-12 mph speed range, and two years
          of parts and one year of labour cover; NordicTrack and Costco agree on the 16 in. pivoting
          touchscreen, the -3% to 12% incline range and the 77.3 x 37 x 59.5 in. footprint. Those
          figures are what earlier pages on this site left out because older listings disagreed;
          they are stated here for NTL17125 only. Figures that appear in a single source are
          labelled as such. We have not tested the Commercial 1750, and none of these numbers are
          our own measurements. Prices are those shown on 14 October 2026 and change constantly. We
          earn a commission if you buy through the Amazon link on this page; it does not change what
          we say about the machine.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10">
      <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6">
        <h2 class="flex items-center gap-2 text-lg font-black text-gray-900 mt-0 mb-4">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-5 h-5 text-[#FF5A1F]" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M4 6h16M4 12h16M4 18h7"></path></svg>
          In This Guide
        </h2>
        <nav class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-2">
          <a href="#short-answer" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">1. NordicTrack Commercial 1750 Treadmill: The Short Answer</a>
          <a href="#which-1750" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">2. Which Commercial 1750? Why Older Reviews Disagree</a>
          <a href="#current-specs" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">3. The Specifications NordicTrack Confirms</a>
          <a href="#motor" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">4. The 4.25 CHP Motor, and Why the Warranty Says More</a>
          <a href="#deck" class="flex items-start gap-2 text-[#0F62FE] no-underline font-medium text-sm hover:underline">5. Deck, Cushioning and the 400 lb Rating</a>
